We're excited to release our latest guide: "The Art of Chair Repair: From Loose Joints to Restoration". This comprehensive workshop guide covers the basics of identifying and fixing common chair problems, as well as creative ways to repurpose old chair parts to create unique and functional pieces.

Complete with detailed step-by-step instructions and 100+ photographs, this guide is perfect for:

- DIY enthusiasts looking to breathe new life into their favorite chairs
- Furniture restorers seeking to learn new techniques and materials
- Woodworkers who want to expand their skill set and tackle more complex projects
- Anyone who wants to reduce waste and extend the life of their furniture

In this guide, you'll learn:

1. How to inspect and identify common chair problems, such as loose joints, broken legs, and worn-out seats.
2. Techniques for fixing loose joints, including the use of wood glue, clamps, and joinery methods.
3. How to strengthen broken legs and repair damaged chair frames.
4. Creative ways to repurpose old chair parts, such as turning chair spindles into coat racks or upcycling worn-out seats into new planters.
5. Best practices for refinishing and reupholstering worn-out chair parts, including sanding, staining, and reupholstering techniques.
6. Tips for maintaining and protecting your newly restored chair, including cleaning and polishing methods.

Whether you're a seasoned DIY pro or just starting to explore the world of furniture restoration, "The Art of Chair Repair" has something for everyone. So, get ready to dust off your workshop tools and give your favorite chair the TLC it deserves!

